SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Summary: Add "(macfixes)" to the version string and warn that this is a testing build
Category: system
Kind: feature
Origin: wine-staging
From: wine-staging patches/Staging/0001-ntdll-Print-a-warning-message-specifying-the-wine-st.patch and 0002-winelib-Append-Staging-at-the-end-of-the-version-s.patch (Sebastian Lackner), current wine-staging master (11.x), with this project's name instead of staging's
Source: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine-staging/-/tree/master/patches/Staging (checkout of 2026-11-12, upstream-commit 7384c8babcaa)
Upstream: no
Why: Marks the build as patched: the version string reads "wine-11.21 (macfixes)", and staging's once-per-session warning says this is a testing version and where to report bugs (this project, not WineHQ or Sikarugir: this is not Sikarugir's build).
      Names: WINE_BUILD_NAME/WINE_BUG_REPORTS_TO in dlls/ntdll/loader.c, and the " (macfixes)" suffix in configure.ac and configure (both patched, so no autoreconf is needed).
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: the same mechanism, branded "wine-10.0 (Sikarugir)" and "wine-sikarugir %s is a testing version containing experimental patches."
Port: to 11.21: source is wine-staging master's 11.x form of the two patches; the only change from the 10.0 patch is staging's newer NtClose() of the event handle in the "already warned" branch.
Applies to: wine 11.22

